{# Non-uniform (per-tap) coefficient width FIR template.                      #}
{# The symmetric-folded *structure* is identical for uniform and non-uniform   #}
{# designs — only the per-coefficient bit widths differ. Both modes therefore  #}
{# share a single RTL template (fir_symmetric.v.j2) so the arithmetic,        #}
{# rounding and saturation logic cannot silently drift between the two paths   #}
{# being compared. This wrapper exists solely as a named entry point so that   #}
{# rtlgen.py can distinguish the two code paths without any template logic     #}
{# duplication.                                                                #}
{% include "fir_symmetric.v.j2" %}
